    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "• AMERICAN\nOVERSEAS AIRLY\nAMERICAN",
      "AOA-AMERICAN OVERSEAS AIRLINES\nBoeing 377 Stratocruiser\nAOA, a wholly owned subsidiary of American Airlines,\ninaugurated Stratocruiser service on its New York-\nLondon route on August 17th, 1949, with\ntwo of\nthese aircraft. One of\nthese,\nnamed\nthe \"Flagship\nGreat Britain\",\nis shown on this card. Early in\n1950 the airline's eighth and last 377 had joined\nthe fleet which linked New York and Boston with\n•and Boston\nEngland, Scotland and Scandinavia.\nSeptember 22, 1950 marked AOA's last flights, its\nroutes and aircraft having been sold to another air-\nline.\nPhoto courtesy Boeing Commercial Airplane Company\nPublished by Aviation World, Inc., P.O. Box 188, Bethel, Conn. 06801 U.S.A.\nN90941 c/n 15957\nB-013\n65838-D\npost card\n2015.166.0293"
